{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implementation will be written in standard Go following standard Hyperledger Fabric repository patterns and protobuf definitions (using standard fabric-protos-go).",
    "U1 will involve updating the chaincode simulation read-set structure and peer validation logic (valtrans/committer) to include state values alongside key/version and compare incoming transaction read-set values with the validating peer's state.",
    "U2 through U8 will be organized as a modular, standalone Go library package (e.g., configtx subpackage) with zero external dependency on Viper config loading or network endpoints.",
    "Cryptographic operations will accept standard standard-library types (e.g., crypto.Signer, x509.Certificate, ecdsa.PrivateKey) directly to avoid filesystem or environment assumptions."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The target Hyperledger Fabric codebase version is v2.x.",
    "Development and testing environment includes standard Fabric development prerequisites (Docker, Go SDK/toolchain, protobuf compiler).",
    "All effort estimates assume standard developer unit testing, integration testing, and documentation as part of each activity."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-1",
      "activity_name": "U1: Peer Read-Set Value Inclusion and Tampered State Validation",
      "activity_description": "Extend read-set serialization during simulation to record values alongside key versions. Modify peer transaction validation pipeline to inspect read-set values against local world state to detect tampered endorsing peers and invalidate affected transactions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-2",
      "activity_name": "U2: Standalone CreateChannelTx Library Function",
      "activity_description": "Create Go struct definitions decoupled from Viper/YAML and implement CreateChannelTx to produce proto-encoded channel genesis blocks/creation transactions matching configtxgen outputs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 28
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-3",
      "activity_name": "U3: Detached ChannelUpdate Signature Generation",
      "activity_description": "Implement standalone library function accepting arbitrary cryptographic key material and a serialized ChannelUpdate/Header to construct and output a detached ConfigSignature struct.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-4",
      "activity_name": "U4: ConfigUpdate Envelope Signature Assembly",
      "activity_description": "Implement library function taking a ConfigUpdate transaction and a set of detached signatures to package a fully signed HeaderType_CONFIG_UPDATE envelope ready for submission.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-5",
      "activity_name": "U5: Batch Size (max_message_count) Config Update Generator",
      "activity_description": "Implement library function to generate unsigned channel config update transactions specifically modifying the Orderer BatchSize max_message_count parameter.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-6",
      "activity_name": "U6: Organization ConfigGroup Generator from Raw Crypto Inputs",
      "activity_description": "Implement library function generating an Organization ConfigGroup directly from in-memory X.509/MSP crypto structs, producing identical proto output to configtxgen -printOrg.",
      "most_likely_effort": 18
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-7",
      "activity_name": "U7: Standalone In-Memory ConfigUpdate Diff Compute Engine",
      "activity_description": "Implement pure Go diff calculation engine comparing base and modified Config trees to generate a semantically equivalent ConfigUpdate without needing configtxlator binary.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-8",
      "activity_name": "U8: Consortium Org Addition Config Update Helper",
      "activity_description": "Implement helper function taking system channel configuration and an Org ConfigGroup, producing an unsigned ConfigUpdate transaction adding the organization to a specified consortium.",
      "most_likely_effort": 18
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-9",
      "activity_name": "End-to-End Integration, Parity Verification, and Test Suite",
      "activity_description": "Develop automated integration test suite validating binary parity between library outputs and existing Fabric CLI tools (configtxgen, configtxlator, signtx) and verifying tampered state rejection on a live fabric network.",
      "most_likely_effort": 30
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 208
  }
}
```

